lockdep: make the PROVE_RAW_LOCK_NESTING prompt unconditional

arm64 selects ARCH_SUPPORTS_RT, which hides this option's prompt and
forces it to its `default y` whenever PROVE_LOCKING is enabled — a plain
config disable is silently reverted by olddefconfig. The checker models
PREEMPT_RT wait-type nesting the rewrite drivers deliberately do not
target yet, and its first report disables lockdep for the rest of the
boot. Restoring the prompt lets the ysp debug instrumentation fragment
turn it off. Staged for debug flavors only; production builds never see
this patch.

diff --git a/lib/Kconfig.debug b/lib/Kconfig.debug
index 713cc94caa02e..820976683146a 100644
--- a/lib/Kconfig.debug
+++ b/lib/Kconfig.debug
@@ -1411,7 +1411,7 @@ config PROVE_LOCKING
 	 For more details, see Documentation/locking/lockdep-design.rst.
 
 config PROVE_RAW_LOCK_NESTING
-	bool "Enable raw_spinlock - spinlock nesting checks" if !ARCH_SUPPORTS_RT
+	bool "Enable raw_spinlock - spinlock nesting checks"
 	depends on PROVE_LOCKING
 	default y if ARCH_SUPPORTS_RT
 	help
